  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kvinna till Kvinna Reg MENA and Syria Programme - Kvinna till Kvinna Syria</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kvinna till Kvinna Regionalt MENA och Syrien-prog</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kvinna till Kvinna har presenterat en ans&#xf6;kan f&#xf6;r kvinnors r&#xe4;ttigheter i Mellan&#xf6;stern, Nordafrika och Syrien f&#xf6;r fem &#xe5;r 2017-2021 som omfattar runt 204 700 000 SEK d&#xe4;r Sida kommer att g&#xe5; in med 177 200 000 SEK. St&#xf6;det &#xe4;r en forts&#xe4;ttning p&#xe5; och expandering av tidigare av Sida finansierat MENA- och Syrien- program. MENA-st&#xf6;det uppg&#xe5;r till 111 600 000 SEK och Syrien 65 600 000 SEK. 

Verksamheten kommer att bedrivas i ett flertal l&#xe4;nder i MENA f&#xf6;r det regionala st&#xf6;det  (Jordanien, Libanon, Egypten, Irak och Tunisien) samt f&#xf6;r Syriendelen, Syrien, Libanon och Turkiet d&#xe4;r det syriska civilsamh&#xe4;llet befinner sig. Kvinna till Kvinna kommer att vidarebefordra runt 50 % av st&#xf6;det till sina lokala partners i regionen att genomf&#xf6;ra deras verksamhet inom olika tematiska omr&#xe5;den men med fokus p&#xe5; j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och kvinnors r&#xe4;ttigheter. Insatsen innefattar ocks&#xe5; mycket st&#xf6;d till kapacitetsutveckling, b&#xe5;de tematisk och organisatorisk samt fokus p&#xe5; p&#xe5;verkansarbete inom FN Resolutionen 1325.

Insatsen kommer att finansieras fr&#xe5;n den regionala MENA-strategin samt fr&#xe5;n Syrienkris-strategin.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Program for Women&apos;s Rights in the Middle East and North Africa and Syria. 

The activities will be carried out in several countries in MENA for the regional support (Jordan, Lebanon, Egypt, Iraq and Tunisia) as well as for the Syrian part, Syria, Lebanon and Turkey where the Syrian civil society is located. Kvinna till Kvinna will forward around 50% of the support to its local partners in the region to carry out their activities in different thematic areas but with a focus on gender equality and women&apos;s rights. The effort also includes a lot of support for capacity development, both thematic and organizational, as well as a focus on advocacy work within UN Resolution 1325.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the intervention is to achieve increased capacity of women&apos;s rights organisations and women&apos;s human rights defenders to contribute to strengthening women&apos;s participation and the respect and advancement of women&apos;s rights. For the MENAFEM programme there have been four outcomes
formulated: 
1. Strenghtened women&apos;s organisations. 
2. Advocacy for changes to law, policy and practice that promote women&apos;s rights and gender equality and an enabling environment for women&apos;s human rights
defenders. 
3. Prevention of and protection against gender-based violence. 
4. Increased women&apos;s political participation.</narrative>
  </description>
